  // Same logic as updatePlaneWorldPosition but with configurable lerpFactor
  // ... (same back-projection logic) ...
  planeGroup.position.lerp(targetPosition, lerpFactor);
}
```

Then have `updatePlaneWorldPosition` call `updatePlaneWorldPositionWithLerp(centerFeature, 0.5)` for backward compatibility, or replace all calls.

#### 2f. Adaptive ComplementaryFilter alpha (in `updateCameraFromIMU`, around line 1360)

Currently the visual confidence is passed to `complementaryFilter.fuse()`. Enhance this to also consider feature quality state:

```typescript
// In updateCameraFromIMU, before the fuse call:
if (this.featureQualityMonitor) {
  const qualityState = this.featureQualityMonitor.getState();
  if (qualityState === FeatureQualityState.DROUGHT) {
    // Override: near-pure IMU
    this.complementaryFilter.updateAlpha(0.0); // forces alpha toward 0.99
  } else if (qualityState === FeatureQualityState.POOR) {
    this.complementaryFilter.updateAlpha(0.3); // balanced
  }
  // RICH: let existing logic handle it based on visual confidence
